in the far southwest of Westeros at the  mouth of the river honey wine lies the  great stone city of Old Town it is home  to the Citadel where men and boys from  throughout the kingdoms come to receive  their training as maesters maesters play  an integral role in Westeros a society  serving as scholars healers and advisors  to the nobility of the Seven Kingdoms  this venerable  order of learnin men dedicate their  lives to serving the realm and us warned  to occupy a neutral position when it  comes to power and politics upon  completing his training of the Citadel  and taking his vows a maester renounces  his family name and takes a vow of  celibacy he is assigned to a castle or  keep and duty-bound to serve as its  counsellor and healer even if control of  the castle changes hands and maces  allegiance is to the realm not to any  one family his badge of office is a  great chain forged from links of  different metals which he wears around  his neck it is a reminder of his role as  a servant of the realm and is never to  be removed a maester forges his chain  with study and each link represents the  mastery of a different kind of learning  for instance the Silberling signifies  mastery of the medicinal arts a golden  link represents the study of money and  accounting an iron link indicates  knowledge of Warcraft Raven ray is an  especially important skill for a maester  as it is he who breeds trains and  maintains carrier Ravens for the  delivering of messages throughout the  land  there are some masters who have earned a  link forged of Valyrian steel this  signifies knowledge of the higher  mysteries commonly known as magic only  one maester in a hundred possesses such  a link as this feel of study is frowned  upon by many in the order it is possible  magic may have existed for a time not  long ago but most consider the higher  mysteries to be long gone from this  world service as a maester is a noble  calling  one of vital importance to a prosperous  realm it is little wonder there are some  who refer to the order as the Knights of  the mind
 

